IMPORT prelude

-- Significant Infrastructure Government Loan Act 2021 (Singapore) -- what counts as nationally significant infrastructure (s 2),
-- the borrowing limits (s 5), where the money goes (s 10), which projects and which spending qualify (s 11), and what a holder of a
-- security issued under the Act gets: redemption, early redemption, interest and when it stops (ss 12-15), the securities lending
-- cap (s 18), and transfers of book-entry securities through the MAS (ss 20-22).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation -- version in force from 29 May 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SIGLA2021.txt. The latest
-- amendment annotated is Act 8 of 2026 (Coastal Protection and Other Amendments Act 2026), in force 29 May 2026, which added
-- coastal management to the purposes in s 2.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0205 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The person the Act meets is an investor holding its securities; the rest of it binds the Minister.
-- SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: the foreign-currency conversion rules (s 5(5)), the yield-to-maturity arithmetic behind the
-- interest threshold (s 5(3)) -- the encoding takes the effective-interest total as given --, issuing powers and charges on the
-- Consolidated Fund (ss 6-8), the MAS's agency and depositary functions (ss 17, 19), confirmation advices (s 23), and Regulations
-- (ss 24, 25). No Regulations made under the Act were retrieved.
--
-- Dates are written as numbers of the form YYYYMMDD (3 August 2021 is 20210803), which keeps their order.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Significant Infrastructure Government Loan Act 2021`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- nationally significant infrastructure`

-- s 2: "nationally significant infrastructure" means any structure or building in Singapore that (a) "is or is intended to be
-- controlled and legally owned by the Government"; (b) is primarily for (i) transport by road or rail, air, sea or inland waterway;
-- (ii) sewage or water; (iii) "the alleviation of floods"; (iv) coastal management [Act 8 of 2026 wef 29/05/2026]; (v) energy;
-- (vi) telecommunications, broadcasting and data; (vii) "any other purpose ... in which initial or further investment is vital to
-- supporting, or is likely to materially improve, national productivity or Singapore's economic, environmental or social
-- sustainability"; and (c) "is or is intended principally for use by (whether or not free) or for the benefit of ... the general
-- public in Singapore".
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `transport`
    `sewage or water`
    `flood alleviation`
    `coastal management`
    `energy`
    `telecommunications or data`
    `another purpose vital to national productivity or sustainability`
    `none of the listed purposes`

GIVEN `in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `controlled and legally owned by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A Purpose,
      `principally for the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is nationally significant infrastructure` IF
        `in Singapore`
    AND `controlled and legally owned by the Government`
    AND `principally for the general public`
    AND CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `none of the listed purposes` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2: "related facility" -- a structure, building, fitting, fixture, plant, computer or other system without which the
-- infrastructure would not have a useful life of at least 50 years, could not operate for its purpose, or would cease to be
-- nationally significant infrastructure, "regardless of the useful life of the related facility itself, but does not include any
-- train, vehicle or vessel". Examples: pumping stations are; airbridges are; "Rolling stock, locomotives, aircraft and barges are
-- not".
DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `a fixed structure or system`
    `a train, vehicle or vessel`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing, `the infrastructure depends on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a related facility` IF
        `the infrastructure depends on it`
    AND CONSIDER `the thing`
        WHEN `a train, vehicle or vessel` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5 -- borrowing limits`

-- s 5(1): the Minister "must not raise a loan" if (a) the total at any time of (i) the proposed borrowing and (ii) "the total amount
-- of sums borrowed under any loan earlier raised under this Act" EXCEEDS $90,000,000,000; or (b) the total effective interest paid
-- or payable within the relevant period (the previous financial year, s 5(4)) on all outstanding securities "is more than the
-- interest threshold amount of $5,000,000,000".
-- s 5(2): (1)(a) does not apply to (a) a borrowing that the Minister "(in person)" designates as refinancing a previous borrowing
-- under the Act AND "is for a sum less than the total amount of securities issued under this Act and redeemed or with a maturity
-- date within the same year"; nor to (b) securities loaned by the MAS under s 18 or held by it for that purpose.
-- (1)(a)(ii) counts sums BORROWED, not sums outstanding: the text does not deduct redemptions. That reading is the encoding's.
GIVEN `designated in person as refinancing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the proposed sum` IS A NUMBER, `redeemed or maturing this year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refinancing exception applies` IF
    `designated in person as refinancing` AND `the proposed sum` LESS THAN `redeemed or maturing this year`

GIVEN `the proposed sum` IS A NUMBER, `earlier borrowings` IS A NUMBER, `of which lent by the MAS` IS A NUMBER,
      `designated in person as refinancing` IS A BOOLEAN, `redeemed or maturing this year` IS A NUMBER,
      `effective interest last financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may raise the loan` IF
        (     `the refinancing exception applies` `designated in person as refinancing` `the proposed sum` `redeemed or maturing this year`
          OR  `the proposed sum` PLUS `earlier borrowings` MINUS `of which lent by the MAS` AT MOST 90000000000)
    AND `effective interest last financial year` AT MOST 5000000000

-- s 9: "Despite anything in the Interpretation Act 1965 or any other law, the Minister must not delegate the Minister's power under
-- this Part."
GIVEN `raised by the Minister personally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power was validly exercised` IF `raised by the Minister personally`

§§ `10 -- where the money goes`

-- s 10(1): the face value of every security, "less any sum mentioned in section 5(2)", (a) "must be paid into the Development Fund";
-- and (b) "may only be appropriated to meet nationally significant infrastructure expenditure by the Government".
GIVEN `the face value` IS A NUMBER, `the section 5(2) sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount paid into the Development Fund` MEANS `the face value` MINUS `the section 5(2) sum`

§§ `11 -- which projects and which spending qualify`

-- s 11(2): an "infrastructure project" is (a) construction or acquisition of nationally significant infrastructure; (b) building,
-- installing or acquiring a related facility; (c) improvement, extension, enlargement or replacement that significantly
-- (i) increases capacity or reliability, (ii) increases useful life or (iii) reduces previously assessed operating costs -- "such that
-- the nationally significant infrastructure has or has left, or is reasonably expected to have or have left, a useful life of at
-- least 50 years upon the completion of the infrastructure project". The "such that" clause stands flush left in the deposit, so
-- the encoding applies it to (a), (b) and (c) alike. That is a reading of the layout.
DECLARE ProjectKind IS ONE OF
    `construction or acquisition`
    `a related facility`
    `a significant upgrade`
    `a minor upgrade`
    `repair or maintenance only`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A ProjectKind, `useful life on completion in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an infrastructure project` IF
        `useful life on completion in years` AT LEAST 50
    AND CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `a minor upgrade` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `repair or maintenance only` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 11(5): the Minister "must not approve any infrastructure project" unless (a) the total qualifying capital expenditure "is
-- estimated to be $4,000,000,000 or more"; and (b) the project "is ongoing on, or starts on or after 3 August 2021". s 11(7):
-- "approved" means "approved in person by the Minister".
GIVEN `it is a project` IS A BOOLEAN, `estimated qualifying expenditure` IS A NUMBER, `ongoing on or starting after 3 August 2021` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approved by the Minister in person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the project is approved` IF
        `it is a project`
    AND `estimated qualifying expenditure` AT LEAST 4000000000
    AND `ongoing on or starting after 3 August 2021`
    AND `approved by the Minister in person`

-- s 11(6): where a project is split into distinct contracts, a contract for anything that (a) "is capable of being completed and to
-- start operations independently" of the others AND (b) "is situated on lands that are not adjacent or contiguous" "must be
-- disregarded" in estimating the total.
GIVEN `the main contracts` IS A NUMBER, `a separate contract` IS A NUMBER, `separate contract stands alone` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `separate contract on non-adjacent land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the estimate for the threshold` MEANS
    IF `separate contract stands alone` AND `separate contract on non-adjacent land`
    THEN `the main contracts`
    ELSE `the main contracts` PLUS `a separate contract`

-- s 11(3): "qualifying capital expenditure" is capital expenditure by an infrastructure project participant "wholly or
-- substantially" for the project, "and even if incurred before 3 August 2021"; including (a) rights to use an invention,
-- (b) design, investigative and engineering studies, survey or research, (c) works bringing the infrastructure to its location and
-- condition. (4) EXCLUDES (a) repair or maintenance; (b) "the acquisition of land and of any right or interest in or over land";
-- (c) "the acquisition, repair or maintenance of any train, vehicle, aircraft, vessel or barge".
-- s 11(7): a participant is the ministry, department or Organ of State responsible, or "a public authority carrying out the
-- infrastructure project as an agent or otherwise on behalf of" it.
DECLARE Spending IS ONE OF
    `construction works`
    `a licence to use an invention`
    `design and engineering studies`
    `works to bring it into operating condition`
    `repair or maintenance`
    `buying the land`
    `buying trains or vessels`

DECLARE Spender IS ONE OF
    `the responsible ministry`
    `a public authority on the ministry's behalf`
    `a public authority on its own account`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the spending` IS A Spending, `the spender` IS A Spender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is qualifying capital expenditure` IF
        CONSIDER `the spender`
        WHEN `the responsible ministry` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a public authority on the ministry's behalf` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    AND CONSIDER `the spending`
        WHEN `repair or maintenance` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `buying the land` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `buying trains or vessels` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 11(1): "nationally significant infrastructure expenditure" is qualifying capital expenditure "incurred, on or after 3 August 2021,
-- in relation to an approved infrastructure project". Read with s 11(3), spending before that date counts towards the $4 billion
-- threshold but cannot itself be met from the loan (s 10(1)(b)).
GIVEN `it qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN, `the project is approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `incurred on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan may pay for it` IF
    `it qualifies` AND `the project is approved` AND `incurred on` AT LEAST 20210803

§§ `12-15 -- what the holder gets`

-- s 12: a security "is redeemable at par on" (a) its maturity date; or (b) if "redeemable at the election of the holder", on the
-- earlier of (i) the redemption date in the holder's notice to the MAS and (ii) the maturity date.
GIVEN `maturity date` IS A NUMBER, `redeemable at the holder's election` IS A BOOLEAN, `holder gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `date in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the redemption date` MEANS
    IF `redeemable at the holder's election` AND `holder gave notice`
    THEN `the smaller of` `date in the notice` `maturity date`
    ELSE `maturity date`

-- s 13(1), (2): the holder of a security "not redeemable at the election of the holder" may, "upon an invitation of the MAS", apply
-- to redeem early where the MAS has invited the public by public notice and the security is specified or described in it.
-- (4): "the MAS may refuse any application ... without assigning any reason."
GIVEN `redeemable at the holder's election` IS A BOOLEAN, `MAS invited by public notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notice covers this security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder may apply to redeem early` IF
    (NOT `redeemable at the holder's election`) AND `MAS invited by public notice` AND `the notice covers this security`

GIVEN `may apply` IS A BOOLEAN, `the MAS accepts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security is redeemed early` IF `may apply` AND `the MAS accepts`

-- s 14(1): interest "must be paid half-yearly". (2): where a security redeemable at the holder's election "is redeemed before its
-- maturity date, a portion of the half-yearly interest ... (calculated on a pro-rata basis) is payable" on the notice date. The
-- encoding pro-rates by days, which "pro-rata" does not specify.
GIVEN `half-yearly interest` IS A NUMBER, `days elapsed in the period` IS A NUMBER, `days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pro-rata interest` MEANS `half-yearly interest` TIMES `days elapsed in the period` DIVIDED BY `days in the period`

-- s 15: "Regardless of any demand for payment of the principal sum", interest stops immediately after (a) the maturity date; (b) the
-- redemption date in a duly served notice under s 12(b)(i); or (c) the date of early redemption under s 13, "whichever is the
-- earliest".
GIVEN `maturity date` IS A NUMBER, `holder gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `date in the notice` IS A NUMBER, `redeemed early` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `early redemption date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date interest stops` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (IF `holder gave notice` THEN `the smaller of` `date in the notice` `maturity date` ELSE `maturity date`)
        (IF `redeemed early` THEN `early redemption date` ELSE `maturity date`)

§§ `18 -- securities lending cap`

-- s 18(2): securities on loan by the MAS to primary dealers "must not exceed (a) $6,500,000,000; or (b) a higher sum specified by
-- Parliament in a resolution". The encoding takes a resolution figure of 0 to mean no resolution.
GIVEN `on loan` IS A NUMBER, `figure in a Parliament resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lending is within the cap` IF
    `on loan` AT MOST 6500000000 OR `on loan` AT MOST `figure in a Parliament resolution`

§§ `16, 20-22 -- transfers and pledges`

-- s 16: "A holder of a book-entry security may transfer or pledge" it. s 20(1): a transfer or pledge to the MAS, the Government or
-- an eligible account-holder "must be effected, despite any law to the contrary, by the MAS making an appropriate entry in its
-- records". (3): a transfer or pledge so effected "has priority over any transfer or pledge ... effected or created in any other
-- manner before, on or after" it. s 21(1) allows other means; (4): the MAS "must not accept any notice or advice" of a transfer
-- not effected under s 20, "and any such notice or advice is void".
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF
    `an entry in the MAS records`
    `another means`

GIVEN `first transfer` IS A Mode, `second transfer` IS A Mode
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the second transfer wins` IF
    CONSIDER `second transfer`
    WHEN `an entry in the MAS records` THEN
        CONSIDER `first transfer`
        WHEN `an entry in the MAS records` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the mode` IS A Mode
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the MAS may accept notice of it` IF
    CONSIDER `the mode`
    WHEN `an entry in the MAS records` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 22(1): the MAS "is not liable for conversion or for participation in any breach of fiduciary duty" where it acted "according to
-- the instructions of its depositor even though the depositor had no right to dispose of" the securities.
GIVEN `acted on the depositor's instructions` IS A BOOLEAN, `the depositor had the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the MAS is protected from liability` IF `acted on the depositor's instructions`
